\begin{abstract}
The \software{hep-talk} package provides a lightweight slide system for HEP talks.
It sets slide geometry from the requested paper width and aspect ratio, loads the HEP font, math-font, bibliography, title, and text modules, defines block, column, row, frame, and slide environments with overlay support, provides title-logo handling and slide page numbers, and ships dark, light, blue, and metropolis-inspired colour themes.
\end{abstract}
%
\section{Introduction}

The package can be loaded using "\usepackage{hep-talk}".

\DescribeMacro{paperwidth}
\DescribeMacro{ratio}
The size of the slides is adjusted with the "paperwidth="\meta{dimension} option.
The ratio can be adjusted with the "ratio="\meta{fraction} option, for example "ratio=9/16" or "ratio=.5625".

\section{Macros and environments}

\DescribeMacro{\newframe}
New frames can be generated using the "\newframe"\oarg{title} macro.

\DescribeEnv{slide}
\DescribeEnv{robustslide}
The "slide" and "robustslide" environments start a new frame and wrap its contents in the "overlays" environment of the \software{overlays} package \cite{overlays}.
The "robustslide" environment reads its body verbatim, like "fragileoverlays", so that it can contain fragile material such as verbatim text.
Their optional argument becomes the slide title.

\DescribeEnv{block}
The basic building block is the "\begin"\marg{block}\oarg{title} environment, that generates a block with attached title stretching over the whole page.
It accepts a star that switches the overlay behaviour from "only" to "visible", an optional overlay specification, an optional title, and an optional width.

\DescribeEnv{columns}
The "\begin"\marg{columns}\oarg{title}\oarg{column} environment generates space for \meta{column} columns if \meta{column} is an integer and a single column with width \meta{column}"\linewidth" if \meta{column} is smaller than one.
It uses the same star and overlay conventions as "block".

\DescribeMacro{\column}
The "\column"\oarg{title}\oarg{size} macro generates a new column.
It uses the same star and overlay conventions as "block".
In a "columns" environment with an integer \meta{column}, the column is "1/"\meta{size} of the line wide and defaults to "1/"\meta{column}.
Otherwise \meta{size} is the column width as a fraction of the line width and defaults to \meta{column}.

\DescribeMacro{\row}
The "\row"\oarg{title} macro starts a new row in a "block" or "column".

\DescribeMacro{\logo}
\DescribeMacro{\prelogo}
\DescribeMacro{\postlogo}
The "\logo"\marg{code} macro stores title-page logo material.
The "\prelogo" and "\postlogo" hooks adjust the material placed before and after it.

\DescribeMacro{\citestyle}
\DescribeMacro{\cite}
Citations are formatted for slides using the \software{hep-bibliography} setup.
The "\citestyle"\marg{citation} macro typesets small right-aligned citations in the structure colour.
The "\cite" macro applies this style to "\autocite" and takes the same optional prenote and postnote.
Citations show the author and year or the e-print number, also with the default numeric style of \software{hep-bibliography}.

\section{Themes}

The extracted "hep-dark", "hep-light", "hep-blue", and "hep-metropolis" files define the page, title, caption, block, structure, and highlight colours used by the package.
They are loaded after \software{hep-talk}, for example with "\usepackage{hep-dark}".
Without a theme, the colours of "hep-light" are used.

